    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.4,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"short_to_supply\",\n      \"components\": [\"U2\", \"U4\", \"J2\", \"J5\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U2.2\", \"U4.1\", \"J2.1\", \"J5.1\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"NET0019\", \"NET0009\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The 1043 battery holder U2's '\u2212' pin (pin 2) appears to run on a horizontal wire at the NET0019 level to the left, where NET0019 is the same label used for the barrel-jack centre pin J2.1 and J5.1 on the BAT+ rail. The diode U4 cathode is on NET0009, which also reaches the BAT+ bus. The drawing therefore appears to place the battery negative terminal on the positive rail.\",\n      \"expected\": \"Per the spec, the battery negative (U7.2) returns to BAT- and is not joined to BAT+. Only the battery positive should feed BAT+ through the isolation diode U6 (anode on battery, cathode on BAT+).\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"Battery (U7, 18650 holder) \u2192 pin 1 \u2192 Net-(U6-A) \u2192 U6 (SS2040FL) anode\u2192cathode \u2192 BAT+.\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"Since pins 2 and 3 are normally shorted ... and BAT- only otherwise reaches U7.2 (battery negative) and J6.1\"},\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"EthernetAndPower page: U4 SS2040FL with NET0009 and NET0019 labels; U2 1043 with '+' pin 1 and '\u2212' pin 2 on the NET0019 wire at y\u2248732\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If the battery negative terminal is tied to the BAT+ rail, the cell is shorted or its discharge path is broken. The board would fail to run from the battery or would drain it through a short.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.4\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"wrong_value\",\n      \"components\": [\"C2\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"C2.1\", \"C2.2\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"EPD boost output node (U10 cathode / L2 output)\"],\n      \"observed\": \"C2 is labelled 4.7uF/25V, while the spec's EPD table gives the reference 1 \u00b5F/25 V default for this position and 1 \u00b5F/6.3 V for the G1 position.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The spec lists C2 at 1 \u00b5F/25 V (PDI default) and does not mention a 4.7 \u00b5F part in the EPD driver.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"C2 default: 1 \u00b5F/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 \u00b5F/25 V | Matches default\"},\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"EPD_Driver page: C2 with value 4.7uF/25V\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"A larger output capacitor on the boost node changes the boost converter's output ripple and loop behaviour relative to the reference circuit. The effect is likely minor.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.2\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The schematic is largely consistent with the spec, including the FAN53610 wiring (MODE to GND, EN on VIN/VBUS), the SD-card pin share and the EPD circuit. The main concern is that the battery holder's negative pin appears to sit on the NET0019 (BAT+) rail, and the EPD output capacitor value differs from the spec.\"\n}",
